Zak Katz: Let me be clear: S_t shifts _in time_ not in space. So to be clear: let a PDE F(x_1, ..., x_n, t)=0 PDE w.r.t time t,  if u(x,t) is a solution and f_t(x) = u(x,t) is a "state" at time t, and Let S_t be the "time-shift" operator so that S_t(f_a) = f_{a+t} for some state f_a at time a. (NOT the space shift operator f(x) -> f(x+t)). Is S_t always diagonalizable?

