Zak Katz: Okay. Is it a necesssary and sufficient condition that S_t is diagonalizable by the Fourier basis iff the diagonalizable operator is translation invariant? Just to make sure I understand what translation invariant means here, we are talking about _space_ translation, and we mean that if S_t is our operator and \tau_a is our space-translation, then:
\(
S_t(\tau_a(f)) = \tau_a(S_t(f))
